# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yongliang Ou et al. (2024). Atomistic modeling of bulk and grain boundary diffusion in solid electrolyte Li 6 PS 5 Cl using machine-learning interatomic potentials.
#   Physical Review Materials. doi:10.1103/physrevmaterials.8.115407  arXiv:2407.04126v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2407.04126v2 (sha256 f521892c2c84a6e8...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 616 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/ou2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the five final level-18 moment tensor potentials (807
# parameters) trained with the quality-level-based active-learning scheme
# for anion-ordered and anion-disordered bulk Li6PS5Cl and three grain
# boundaries, with the training and (bulk) validation RMSEs of Table III.
# Diffusion coefficients, Arrhenius parameters and structural data are
# property results.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
